  "tutorial_example_entry": {
    "lesson_index": 4,
    "lesson_title": "Transforming Shifted Ramps",
    "lesson_core_move": "Rewrite shifted ramp terms as delayed ramp-and-step components and apply the Laplace time-shifting property to compute their transforms for piecewise-signal representations.",
    "section_count": 5,
    "sections": [
      {
        "lesson_index": 4,
        "lesson_title": "Transforming Shifted Ramps",
        "section_index": 1,
        "section_title": "Introduction to Transforming Shifted Ramps",
        "step_type": "tutorial",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "tutorial_content": {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The key object for this topic is the shifted ramp in delayed causal form: whenever a ramp term can be written as $f(t-a)u(t-a)$, it is ready for one-sided time-shifting. In this lesson, that form is the cue to use the exact transform rule rather than re-deriving an integral each time.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Use the base seed first: the ramp with no shift is $t u(t)$, and its one-sided transform is the reference template for this section.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\mathcal{L}\\{t u(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s^2}",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Now apply the shifted-ramp action in one line: rewrite delayed ramps as $f(t-a)u(t-a)$ and then apply $\\mathcal{L}\\{f(t-a)u(t-a)\\}=e^{-a s}F(s)$. The substitution is $\\tau=t-a$, and that same shift amount $a$ is the one that appears in the exponential multiplier in the transform.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\mathcal{L}\\{f(t-a)u(t-a)\\}=e^{-a s}F(s)",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Before moving to examples, avoid three common failure points: use the wrong sign in the delay ($a$ should match the signal’s activation time), drop the unit step factor $u(t-a)$, or attach $e^{-a s}$ to the wrong base transform term. Keep these checks in this order: verify $a$, verify $f(t-a)$, then verify one-sided support with $u(t-a)$.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 4,
        "lesson_title": "Transforming Shifted Ramps",
        "section_index": 2,
        "section_title": "Transforming a Basic Delayed Ramp",
        "step_type": "example",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "example_content": {
          "example_prompt": "Find $\\mathcal{L}\\{(t-2)u(t-2)\\}$.",
          "explanation_blocks": [
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The cue here is to first make the signal match the delayed canonical form $f(t-a)u(t-a)$; for this example, the expression already has that structure with $a=2$ and local base $f(t)=t$.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "From the base seed, we use the known one-sided transform of a simple ramp:",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\mathcal{L}\\{t u(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s^2}",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Apply the time-shifting theorem directly: multiply the base transform by $e^{-a s}$ with the same delay $a=2$ that appears in the step gate.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\mathcal{L}\\{f(t-a)u(t-a)\\}=e^{-a s}F(s)",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Substitute $f(t)=t$, $a=2$, and $F(s)=1/s^2$ to get",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\mathcal{L}\\{(t-2)u(t-2)\\}=e^{-2s}\\frac{1}{s^2} = \\frac{e^{-2s}}{s^2}",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Keep the delayed-ramp template exactly in this order for the next step: identify $a$, confirm one-sided support with $u(t-a)$, then apply $e^{-a s}$ to the base ramp seed.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 4,
        "lesson_title": "Transforming Shifted Ramps",
        "section_index": 3,
        "section_title": "Transforming a Scaled Delayed Ramp",
        "step_type": "example",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "example_content": {
          "example_prompt": "Find $\\mathcal{L}\\{3(t-4)u(t-4)\\}$.",
          "explanation_blocks": [
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The cue is to match the delayed-ramp template $3(t-4)u(t-4)=3f(t-4)u(t-4)$ with the local seed $f(t)=tu(t)$.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Keep the scalar outside the transform first, so linearity gives the separation of the gain:",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\mathcal{L}\\{3f(t-4)u(t-4)\\}=3\\,\\mathcal{L}\\{f(t-4)u(t-4)\\}",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Then apply the one-sided shift rule to the seed base term. The same delay $a=4$ appears in both the local-time argument and the unit-step gate.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\mathcal{L}\\{f(t-a)u(t-a)\\}=e^{-as}F(s)",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "For $f(t)=tu(t)$, we use the base transform $\\mathcal{L}\\{t u(t)\\}=1/s^2$, then attach the delay factor $e^{-4s}$.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\mathcal{L}\\{3(t-4)u(t-4)\\}=3e^{-4s}\\,\\frac{1}{s^2}=\\frac{3e^{-4s}}{s^2}",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 4,
        "lesson_title": "Transforming Shifted Ramps",
        "section_index": 4,
        "section_title": "Transforming a Delayed Ramp with a Constant Offset",
        "step_type": "example",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "example_content": {
          "example_prompt": "Find $\\mathcal{L}\\{(t-2+5)u(t-2)\\}$.",
          "explanation_blocks": [
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The cue is to put the expression into local delayed pieces so we can apply the same one-sided shift template term by term.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "(t-2+5)u(t-2)=(t-2)u(t-2)+5u(t-2)",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Use linearity to transform each piece separately with the same delay $a=2$.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "For the ramp piece, use the delayed-ramp seed rule:",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\mathcal{L}\\{(t-a)u(t-a)\\}=\\frac{e^{-as}}{s^2},\\quad a\\ge 0",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "For the delayed constant piece, use:",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\mathcal{L}\\{u(t-a)\\}=\\frac{e^{-as}}{s},\\quad a\\ge 0",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Substitute $a=2$ and combine in the same delayed factor form.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\mathcal{L}\\{(t-2+5)u(t-2)\\}=\\frac{e^{-2s}}{s^2}+\\frac{5e^{-2s}}{s}=e^{-2s}\\left(\\frac{1}{s^2}+\\frac{5}{s}\\right)",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "That final factorized form preserves the same delay mechanism while making the ramp and offset contributions explicit.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 4,
        "lesson_title": "Transforming Shifted Ramps",
        "section_index": 5,
        "section_title": "Transforming Sums of Shifted Ramp and Step Terms",
        "step_type": "example",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "example_content": {
          "example_prompt": "Find $\\mathcal{L}\\{(t-2)u(t-2)+4u(t-2)-u(t-5)\\}$.",
          "explanation_blocks": [
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The cue is to separate each delayed term because linearity is valid only after every part is in a shifted canonical form.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Write the signal as a sum of a delayed ramp seed and two delayed constants:",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "(t-2)u(t-2)+4u(t-2)-u(t-5)=1\\cdot (t-2)u(t-2)+4\\,u(t-2)-1\\cdot u(t-5)",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Apply the delayed-ramp rule to the first term with $a=2$ and the delayed-step rule to the two step terms with their own delays.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\mathcal{L}\\{(t-a)u(t-a)\\}=\\frac{e^{-as}}{s^2},\\quad a\\ge0",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\mathcal{L}\\{u(t-a)\\}=\\frac{e^{-as}}{s},\\quad a\\ge0",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Substitute the identified delays and coefficients.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\mathcal{L}\\{(t-2)u(t-2)\\}=\\frac{e^{-2s}}{s^2},\\quad \\mathcal{L}\\{4u(t-2)\\}=\\frac{4e^{-2s}}{s},\\quad \\mathcal{L}\\{u(t-5)\\}=\\frac{e^{-5s}}{s}",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\mathcal{L}\\{(t-2)u(t-2)+4u(t-2)-u(t-5)\\}=\\frac{e^{-2s}}{s^2}+\\frac{4e^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{e^{-5s}}{s}=e^{-2s}\\left(\\frac{1}{s^2}+\\frac{4}{s}\\right)-\\frac{e^{-5s}}{s}",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Keep this structure: transform each delayed piece separately, then combine by common delay factors if possible.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
